{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "742fe9d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Paper Atypicality (z-scores) — journal pairs, from the cached citation graph\n",
    "\n",
    "Uzzi et al. (2013) atypicality for each paper, from the **journal pairs** of the papers it cites, with a\n",
    "year-preserving shuffle null per focal publication-year cohort. Follows the reference implementation\n",
    "`03_Metrics_Calculation/MAG-Atyp-Comb-1990-2000.ipynb` (same shuffle null, journal-type focal papers,\n",
    "`>1000`-reference skip, per-year cohort Z, per-paper median / 10th-percentile). Primary key: `paper_id`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Raw / input data (directory & structure)\n",
    "```\n",
    "E:/Dawoon Jeong/Data/paper_disruption_csr.npz   # cached CSR (built by paper_disruption): out_ptr/out_idx (references), year, uni_mag\n",
    "E:/Dawoon Jeong/Data/scisci_intermediate/main_primary/paper_metadata.sqlite  # papers(paper_id, journal_id, is_journal)\n",
    "```\n",
    "Reference lists come from the cached CSR's out-edges (references); each cited paper contributes its\n",
    "**journal_id** (from sqlite). Focal papers are **journal-type** (`is_journal`) published in `YEAR_RANGE`.\n",
    "Everything is done in **code space** and one **focal-year cohort at a time**, so peak memory is bounded.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Scope:** the reference computes atypicality for a decade (`YEAR_RANGE = (1990, 2000)`); computing all\n",
    "> ~62M papers with the shuffle null is impractical (a single year ≈ 15 min). Change `YEAR_RANGE` to widen.\n",
    "> Requires `paper_disruption_csr.npz` (built by **paper_disruption**).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Metric (formula)\n",
    "For each focal-year cohort, form the **journal pairs** of every paper's references and count co-occurrences\n",
    "`o`; the null shuffles each cited paper's journal among references sharing the same **cited year** within\n",
    "the cohort (`NUM_SHUFFLES` permutations, preserving citing- and cited-year — equivalent to the reference's\n",
    "`(citing_year, cited_year)` rewiring). `z = (o-μ)/σ` per journal pair (**pairs with σ=0 are skipped**,\n",
    "as in the reference). Per paper: `Z_median`, `Z_10pct`, `Z_min` over its pairs, and `n_pairs`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Output (two files)\n",
    "- `notebook/paper/output/paper_z_score.parquet` — `paper_id, Z_median, Z_10pct, Z_min, n_pairs`.\n",
    "- `notebook/paper/output/z_score_pair.parquet` — `code_1, code_2, year, Z_score` (per journal-pair per year).\n",
    "\n",
    "> `tqdm` shows a per-year progress bar."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "defb0fb1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "snapshot: /project/jevans/renli_shared/OpenAlex_2026_Jan_16_Renly_parquet\n",
      "snapshot : /project/jevans/renli_shared/OpenAlex_2026_Jan_16_Renly_parquet\n",
      "cache    : /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache\n",
      "output   : /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/output\n",
      "  consolidated edge table: present\n",
      "  map            6.71 GB  /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache/work_year_source_map.npz\n",
      "  graph         21.62 GB  /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache/paper_graph.npz\n",
      "  csr           27.20 GB  /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache/paper_csr.npz\n",
      "  journal        3.44 GB  /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache/paper_journal.parquet\n",
      "  fos            2.62 GB  /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache/paper_fos.parquet\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os, sys, gc, time\n",
    "import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex')\n",
    "import oa_common as oa\n",
    "ROOT = oa.BASE; OUT = oa.OUT\n",
    "print('snapshot:', oa.ROOT)\n",
    "NUM_SHUFFLES = 10\n",
    "MIN_REFS, MAX_REFS = 2, 1000\n",
    "YEAR_RANGE = (1900, 2020)   # the reference decade; widen at your own cost\n",
    "# Everything below is fed by notebook/referenced_works_w_year.ipynb: it writes the per-work\n",
    "# map (year + source) and the edge table with both years and both source ids, and\n",
    "# oa.load_graph() / oa.load_csr() / oa.build_journal() read those instead of re-walking\n",
    "# renli's tree. Build it once before running this notebook.\n",
    "assert oa.have_consolidated(), (\n",
    "    'run notebook/referenced_works_w_year.ipynb first — it builds the map and edge table')\n",
    "oa.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f6f366fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load cached CSR (references) + journal per code + focal journal papers in range"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "48ff35b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "CSR cache present: /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache/paper_csr.npz\n",
      "CSR: 2,178,823,795 edges, 348,939,837 papers\n",
      "journal cache present: /project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/cache/paper_journal.parquet\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "# CSR references + journal per code. The sqlite papers(journal_id, is_journal) lookup is\n",
    "# replaced by the primary_locations x sources cache; 'journal-type' is sources.type=='journal',\n",
    "# the analogue of MAG DocType=='Journal'.\n",
    "out_ptr, out_idx, in_ptr, in_idx, year, uni_mag = oa.load_csr()\n",
    "n = len(uni_mag); print(f'CSR: {len(out_idx):,} edges, {n:,} papers')\n",
    "\n",
    "oa.build_journal()\n",
    "jr = pd.read_parquet(oa.JOURNAL_PQ, columns=['work_id', 'source_id', 'is_journal'])\n",
    "pid = oa.id_to_code(jr['work_id'])\n",
    "sid = oa.id_to_code(jr['source_id'].str.replace('^S', 'W', regex=True))  # S… -> int, same codec\n",
    "isj = jr['is_journal'].fillna(False).to_numpy()\n",
    "ok0 = (pid >= 0) & (sid >= 0)\n",
    "pid, sid, isj = pid[ok0], sid[ok0], isj[ok0]\n",
    "del jr; gc.collect()\n",
    "\n",
    "i = np.searchsorted(uni_mag, pid); i = np.clip(i, 0, n - 1); ok = uni_mag[i] == pid\n",
    "journal_by_code = np.full(n, -1, np.int64); journal_by_code[i[ok]] = sid[ok]\n",
    "is_journal_code = np.zeros(n, np.bool_); is_journal_code[i[ok]] = isj[ok]\n",
    "del pid, sid, isj, i, ok; gc.collect()\n",
    "print(f'papers with journal: {(journal_by_code >= 0).sum():,} | journal-type: {is_journal_code.sum():,}')\n",
    "\n",
    "focal_codes = np.flatnonzero(is_journal_code).astype(np.int64)\n",
    "if YEAR_RANGE is not None:\n",
    "    yy = year[focal_codes]; focal_codes = focal_codes[(yy >= YEAR_RANGE[0]) & (yy <= YEAR_RANGE[1])]\n",
    "print(f'focal journal papers in {YEAR_RANGE}: {len(focal_codes):,}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e8a80537",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Uzzi atypicality engine — code space, one focal-year cohort at a time"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d5f33465",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import random\n",
    "from itertools import combinations\n",
    "from collections import defaultdict\n",
    "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
    "\n",
    "def atypicality_from_csr(focal_codes, year, out_ptr, out_idx, journal_by_code,\n",
    "                         num_shuffles=10, min_refs=2, max_refs=500, seed=42):\n",
    "    '''Uzzi et al. atypicality in CODE space, streamed per focal-year cohort (bounded memory).\n",
    "    For each focal paper, its journal pairs come from journal_by_code[refs]; the null preserves each\n",
    "    cited paper's year by shuffling journal codes only among references sharing the same cited-year\n",
    "    within the cohort. Returns (work_df[id, Z_*], pair_df[code_1, code_2, year, Z_score]).'''\n",
    "    random.seed(seed); np.random.seed(seed)\n",
    "    fy = year[focal_codes]\n",
    "    order = np.argsort(fy, kind='stable')\n",
    "    fc = focal_codes[order]; fys = fy[order]\n",
    "    uyears, starts = np.unique(fys, return_index=True)\n",
    "    bounds = list(starts) + [len(fc)]\n",
    "    work_rows = []; pair_rows = []\n",
    "    for gi in tqdm(range(len(uyears)), desc='atypicality by year'):\n",
    "        y = int(uyears[gi]); grp = fc[bounds[gi]:bounds[gi + 1]]\n",
    "        # gather this cohort: (focal_code, journal codes, cited-years) with min<=#journaled refs<=max\n",
    "        cohort = []\n",
    "        for F in grp.tolist():\n",
    "            a0, a1 = out_ptr[F], out_ptr[F + 1]\n",
    "            if a1 == a0: continue\n",
    "            refs = out_idx[a0:a1]\n",
    "            jc = journal_by_code[refs]\n",
    "            keep = jc >= 0\n",
    "            k = int(keep.sum())\n",
    "            if k < min_refs or k > max_refs: continue\n",
    "            cohort.append((F, jc[keep].tolist(), year[refs[keep]].tolist()))\n",
    "        if not cohort: continue\n",
    "        # observed pair counts + per-work pair sets\n",
    "        obs = defaultdict(int); work_pairs = {}\n",
    "        for w, codes, cy in cohort:\n",
    "            seen = set()\n",
    "            for a, b in combinations(codes, 2):\n",
    "                p = (a, b) if a <= b else (b, a)\n",
    "                if p not in seen: seen.add(p); obs[p] += 1\n",
    "            work_pairs[w] = list(seen)\n",
    "        # null: shuffle journal codes among references sharing the same cited-year (within cohort)\n",
    "        group_codes = defaultdict(list); slots = []\n",
    "        for wi, (w, codes, cy) in enumerate(cohort):\n",
    "            for c, yy in zip(codes, cy):\n",
    "                group_codes[yy].append(c); slots.append((wi, yy))\n",
    "        null_counts = []\n",
    "        for _ in range(num_shuffles):\n",
    "            shuffled = {k: v[:] for k, v in group_codes.items()}\n",
    "            for k in shuffled: random.shuffle(shuffled[k])\n",
    "            ptr = defaultdict(int); perwork = defaultdict(list)\n",
    "            for wi, yy in slots:\n",
    "                perwork[wi].append(shuffled[yy][ptr[yy]]); ptr[yy] += 1\n",
    "            ec = defaultdict(int)\n",
    "            for wi, codes_s in perwork.items():\n",
    "                seen = set()\n",
    "                for a, b in combinations(codes_s, 2):\n",
    "                    p = (a, b) if a <= b else (b, a)\n",
    "                    if p not in seen: seen.add(p); ec[p] += 1\n",
    "            null_counts.append(ec)\n",
    "        # z per pair (reference MAG-Atyp-Comb skips pairs whose null std == 0)\n",
    "        zmap = {}\n",
    "        for p, o in obs.items():\n",
    "            vals = np.array([nc.get(p, 0) for nc in null_counts], dtype=float)\n",
    "            mu, sd = vals.mean(), vals.std()\n",
    "            if sd == 0.0:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            z = (o - mu) / sd\n",
    "            zmap[p] = z; pair_rows.append((p[0], p[1], y, z))\n",
    "        # per-work aggregates\n",
    "        for w, codes, cy in cohort:\n",
    "            zs = [zmap[p] for p in work_pairs[w] if p in zmap]\n",
    "            if zs:\n",
    "                arr = np.array(zs)\n",
    "                work_rows.append((w, float(np.median(arr)), float(np.percentile(arr, 10)),\n",
    "                                  float(arr.min()), len(arr)))\n",
    "        del cohort, obs, work_pairs, group_codes, slots, null_counts, zmap\n",
    "    work_df = pd.DataFrame(work_rows, columns=['code', 'Z_median', 'Z_10pct', 'Z_min', 'n_pairs'])\n",
    "    pair_df = pd.DataFrame(pair_rows, columns=['code_1', 'code_2', 'year', 'Z_score'])\n",
    "    return work_df, pair_df\n",
    "print('atypicality engine ready (code-space, per-year streaming)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "35b5f121",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Compute (per-year Uzzi) and save both outputs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0b733c0f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "work_df, pair_df = atypicality_from_csr(\n",
    "    focal_codes, year, out_ptr, out_idx, journal_by_code,\n",
    "    num_shuffles=NUM_SHUFFLES, min_refs=MIN_REFS, max_refs=MAX_REFS)\n",
    "work_df['paper_id'] = oa.code_to_id(uni_mag[work_df['code'].to_numpy()])\n",
    "work_df = work_df[['paper_id', 'Z_median', 'Z_10pct', 'Z_min', 'n_pairs']]\n",
    "work_df.to_parquet(f'{OUT}/paper_z_score_260831.parquet', index=False)\n",
    "pair_df.to_parquet(f'{OUT}/z_score_pair_260831.parquet', index=False)\n",
    "print(f'paper_z_score: {len(work_df):,} papers | z_score_pair: {len(pair_df):,} (pair,year) rows')\n",
    "display(work_df.head(10)); display(pair_df.head(10))\n",
    "print(work_df[['Z_median', 'Z_10pct', 'Z_min']].describe())"
   ]
  }
 ],
